title: <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> Congress
subtitle: The economic depression has radicalized the party...
view-if: year = 1930 and month = 11 and traditionalist_leader = "Hargen"
on-arrival: pro_republic += traditionalist_votes if pro_republic < 50
max-visits: 1
tags: event
face-image: img/dnvp3.jpg
new-page: true

= <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> Congress

The victory of the moderates within the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> has not entirely halted the party’s rightward shift since its electoral defeat. Hargen’s triumph over the democratic Young Conservatives, led by Trevannon, has dashed our hopes for a more democratic and constructive <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>.

While the initial turmoil following Mallin’s split and the Serannus Plan has subsided, a rightward shift in the party’s policies remains possible, especially as the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> threatens to eclipse them. The ongoing crisis in the Commonwealth continues to radicalize the electorate—and, by extension, the propertied parties that represent them.

- @statusquo: Hargen has once again won re-election.
- @schiele: The mantle is transferred to Martin Tilford and the <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarians</span>.

@statusquo
choose-if: land_reform == 0 and landed_marcher_normalized < 40 and landed_royalist_normalized < landed_traditionalist_normalized
unavailable-subtitle: The <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarian</span> wing of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">Traditionalists</span> objects, claiming that it is their turn to lead.
on-arrival: hergt_stays_again = 1; landed_traditionalist += 2; landed_royalist += 2; landed_dnf -= 2; burgher_traditionalist -= 1; burgher_royalist += 1; commons_traditionalist -= 1; commons_royalist += 1; faithful_traditionalist -= 1; faithful_unionist += 1; pro_republic -= 4; gold_right += 3; lvp_right += 2
face-image: img/portraits/OskarHergt.jpg

Cuthbert Hargen has been re-elected once again. However, he and the national conservatives within the party are increasingly looking toward alliances with forces to their right, as their previous hostility toward the <span style="color: #003755;">**DNF**</span> continues to fade. Furthermore, the propertied elites influencing the party have pushed its leadership to reconsider some form of cooperation with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>, aiming to integrate them as a "constructive component of the state" through a so-called '<span class="tooltip-text" title="Coined by conservative elites like Staal and Goodryke, this strategy aims to control the dynamic Royalist movement and integrate it into the state by introducing the party to government. In their eyes, this would moderate the Royalists, transforming them into a constructive component of the state.">taming strategy</span>'.

Recently, discussions have emerged about a new referendum—one designed to unite the Commonwealth right, much like the Serannus Plan referendum attempted, but this time focused on prematurely dissolving the Heartland state Assembly. Given the radicalized political climate, such a move would allow the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>, which currently holds a meager [+ royalist_r_heartland +]% of seats, to make significant gains.

@schiele
choose-if: land_reform >= 1 or landed_marcher_normalized >= 30 or landed_royalist_normalized >= landed_traditionalist_normalized
unavailable-subtitle: There is no suitable pretext for a leadership change.
on-arrival: traditionalist_leader = "Tilford"; landed_traditionalist += 6; landed_royalist -= 3; landed_dnf -= 3; landed_traditionalist += landed_other; landed_other = landed_other*0.2; burgher_traditionalist -= 3; burgher_royalist += 3; commons_traditionalist -= 1; commons_royalist += 1; faithful_traditionalist += 7; faithful_other -= 2; faithful_unionist -= 5; unionist_relation -= 5; traditionalist_r += other_r*0.3; other_r = other_r*0.7; gold_right += 3; lvp_right += 2
face-image: img/portraits/schiele.jpg

[? if land_reform >= 1 : Due to the land reform policies enacted by our[? if not marcher_in_government:&nbsp;previous?] government, the <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarian</span> conservative elites have made it their strongest effort to rally the Commonwealth right against them. This involves orchestrating a leadership change within the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>, the primary political home of <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarian</span> conservatism. Cuthbert Hargen has been persuaded to resign, in favor of the president of the Landed League, Martin Tilford. They hope that by electing the most influential figure in the agricultural community, they can safeguard the relevance of organized agriculture within the Commonwealth. ?][? if landed_marcher_normalized >= 30 and land_reform == 0 : With the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> making significant inroads among rural voters, the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> and its <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarian</span> elites have persuaded Cuthbert Hargen to resign, passing the party's leadership to Martin Tilford, the president of the Landed League. They hope that the most influential figure in the agricultural community can stem the tide and maintain the historic bond between agriculture and Commonwealth conservatism in the years ahead. ?][? if landed_royalist_normalized >= landed_traditionalist_normalized and landed_marcher_normalized < 30 and land_reform == 0 : Due to the significant inroads made by the insurgent <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> among their primary rural voter base, the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> and its agrarian elites have persuaded Cuthbert Hargen to step down, passing the party’s leadership to Martin Tilford, president of the Landed League. They hope that the most influential figure in the agricultural community can stem the tide and maintain the historic bond between organized agriculture and Commonwealth conservatism in the years ahead. ?]

Tilford’s election has led to the merger of the majority of the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span> into the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>, strengthening its hold on the countryside and uniting the Landed League in lobbying for <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarian</span> interests. This consolidation has given rise to the renewal of the <span style="color: #385A38;">Green Front</span>, an umbrella group of the Landed League, peasant Free Guilds, and some Faithful and [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]-affiliated agricultural organizations.